// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 99 — Local overrides  (per-machine, NOT tracked by git)
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Copy this file to `99-local.kdl` next to it; that name is gitignored, so what
// you put there stays on this machine and never shows up in `git status`.
// install/bootstrap.sh does the copy for you.
//
// This file is included LAST, and for binds and environment variables the last
// definition wins — so anything here overrides the rest of config.d/ without
// editing tracked files. Verified on niri 26.04.
//
// `output` blocks do NOT work that way and do not belong here: niri resolves an
// output with .iter().find(), so the FIRST block naming a connector wins, and
// one written here would lose to 90-user-extra.kdl silently. Put those in
// config.d/05-local-output.kdl, which is included first for exactly this
// reason.
//
// `include` fails hard on a missing file, which is why the empty copy exists at
// all rather than being created only when you want an override.
//
// Example — a different file manager on this machine only (the repo ships
// Dolphin; this would put nautilus on Super+E here and nowhere else):
//
//   binds {
//       Super+E hotkey-overlay-title="Open the File Manager: nautilus" {
//           spawn "nautilus"
//       }
//   }
//
//   environment {
//       QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME "qt6ct"
//   }
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
